# Vulnerabilities ignored by Trivy. Each entry must carry a reason.
# Revisit whenever the scan turns red: drop entries whose fixed package has
# landed in the Debian suite the runner image tracks (bookworm-security).

# Chromium vulnerabilities fixed upstream in 154.0.8037.57. bookworm-security
# already publishes the patched backport, 154.0.8037.57-1~deb12u1, and the image
# installs it. Trivy's Debian data still lists 154.0.8037.57-1 as the fixed
# version, and `~deb12u1` sorts before `-1`, so it reports the patched build as
# vulnerable. Drop these entries once Trivy records 154.0.8037.57-1~deb12u1 as
# the bookworm fix.
# Chromium is present solely to render Open Graph images. It renders markup the
# server builds from fixed templates, with only server-signed, HTML-escaped text
# interpolated in and fonts inlined as data URIs. It never navigates to a remote
# page, loads no extensions, and shows no browser UI.
CVE-2026-95282
CVE-2026-95293
CVE-2026-95301
CVE-2026-95304
CVE-2026-95306
CVE-2026-95315
CVE-2026-95324
CVE-2026-95333
CVE-2026-95347
CVE-2026-95351
CVE-2026-95354
CVE-2026-95355
CVE-2026-95373
CVE-2026-95380

# Expat vulnerabilities fixed in 2.5.0-1+deb12u4, which Debian has not published
# for bookworm yet: bookworm-security still ships 2.5.0-1+deb12u3, so
# `apt-get upgrade` in server/Dockerfile has no patched package to install.
# libexpat1 is only a transitive dependency of system packages. The server
# parses XML (JUnit reports, S3 and Azure Blob responses) with Saxy and SweetXml,
# which are pure Erlang and don't link libexpat.
# Drop these entries once bookworm-security publishes 2.5.0-1+deb12u4.
CVE-2024-28757
CVE-2025-59375
CVE-2026-25210
CVE-2026-45186
CVE-2026-66046
CVE-2026-93990
